// ICF codes, Socialstyrelsen inventory to SNOMED CT mappings, codes b2-b24
// Several sources map to the same target; each mapping is its own assertion.
context {
    collection "icf-snomed-ct" version="2026.1"
    source system="ICF" release="2026"
    target system="SNOMED_CT" release="20251130"
}
defaults {
    mappings {
        preference "primary"
        assessment-method "source-default-granularity"
    }
}
mapping "b2.1" source="b2" target="SNOMED_CT:106148006" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b2 SNOMED CT 106148006 = ICF chapter b2 Sensory functions and pain (the entire sensory/pain
        chapter: b210 Vision, b215 Sensations related to the eye, b220 Hearing, b230 Vestibular, b235
        Proprioceptive, b240 Sensation of pain, b250-b279 other senses). Target SNOMED CT 4024711 (sctid
        106148006) =, active standard, the direct SNOMED CT observable for sensory function. Broader
        (multi-level): every b2 sensory sub-function is a sensory function, and the SNOMED CT concept fully
        subsumes the sensory axis of b2, but it does not cover the pain axis (ICF b2 uniquely bundles —
        pain is modeled in SNOMED CT as a separate sensation/feeling, e.g. 816065002). So the target is a
        true ancestor for most of b2 but does not fully subsume the whole b2 bundle. Low tier :
        defensible chapter-level ancestor lead (the SNOMED CT sensory-function observable is the closest
        standard concept to the ICF b2 chapter title), but loose because (a) the source bundles pain
        which the target does not subsume and (b) a chapter root is classification scaffolding. Recorded
        as broader rather than no_match because is a direct, defensible term-and-scope match for the
        dominant (sensory) axis of b2 and is the chapter-level standard concept a reviewer would expect.
        """
}
mapping "b210.1" source="b210" target="SNOMED_CT:281004000" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b210 SNOMED CT 281004000 (Syn) = ICF b210 Seeing functions: the sensory functions of the eye
        and related structures — visual function as a sense. Target SNOMED CT 4094031 (sctid 281004000) =,
        active RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (visual function as a
        sensory/physiological function of the eye). Note 61402003 was inactivated (invalid_reason=D,
        2006) and 281004000 is its active successor; 405183003 is a status-evaluation observable, not
        the function itself. 281004000 is the active function-level observable matching b210. High tier
        : exact term match and clear concept equivalence verified in both mirrors via the
        sctid_to_athena_id crosswalk, but no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified, so snapped just
        below. mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
mapping "b210-b229.1" source="b210-b229" target="SNOMED_CT:281004000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b210-b229 SNOMED CT 281004000 = ICF block-range anchor for the block (b210 Seeing + b215
        Sensations related to the eye and adjoining functions) — a classification range/heading, not a
        single clinical concept. The best available standard target is the vision function observable.
        Target SNOMED CT 4094031 (sctid 281004000) =, active. Broader: the target fully subsumes the b210
        vision axis but only partially covers b215 (sensations related to the eye — discomfort, dryness
        etc. — which are not all); the range anchor is also classification scaffolding, not a clinical
        concept. Low tier : defensible as the closest standard concept for the dominant vision axis of
        the range, but loose because it does not cover the b215 eye-sensation axis and the source is a
        range heading. Recorded as broader to preserve the lead for the vision axis a reviewer would
        expect; the b210 and b215 children get their own tighter proposals.
        """
}
mapping "b2100.1" source="b2100" target="SNOMED_CT:363983007" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b2100 SNOMED CT 363983007 (Synskärpa) = ICF b2100 Acuity functions: the visual functions of
        sensing form and contour at given distances — visual acuity as a sensory function. Target SNOMED CT
        4239582 (sctid 363983007) =, active RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical
        concept (visual acuity as an observable visual function), literal FSN term match. High tier :
        exact term match and clear concept equivalence verified in both mirrors via the
        sctid_to_athena_id crosswalk, but no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified, so snapped just
        below. mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
mapping "b21000.1" source="b21000" target="SNOMED_CT:251742009" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b21000 SNOMED CT 251742009 = ICF b21000 Binocular acuity of distant vision: the acuity
        function of both eyes together for far/distance vision. Target SNOMED CT 4089821 (sctid 251742009)
        =, active RF2 production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (binocular distance
        visual acuity as an observable), literal FSN term match (binocular + distance). High tier :
        exact term match and clear concept equivalence verified in both mirrors, no independent Athena
        crosswalk re-verified. mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
mapping "b21001.1" source="b21001" target="SNOMED_CT:251739003" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b21001 SNOMED CT 251739003 = ICF b21001 Monocular acuity of distant vision: the acuity
        function of one eye for far/distance vision (eye-unspecified — left OR right). Target SNOMED CT
        4090514 (sctid 251739003) =, active RF2 production. Broader: SNOMED CT's active monocular
        distance-acuity observables are eye-laterality-specific (386714003, 386716001; the older
        251740001/251741002 are inactive/D). The ICF source is laterality-unspecified (either eye), so
        no single eye-specific SNOMED CT concept matches; 251739003 is the broader, laterality-agnostic
        parent that fully subsumes the monocular-distance axis. Low tier : defensible best-available
        broader target, but real doubt — the target is a deeper climb and also covers binocular distance
        acuity, and there is no independent crosswalk. (Rejecting a single eye-specific concept would
        silently assert laterality the source withholds.)
        """
}
mapping "b21002.1" source="b21002" target="SNOMED_CT:251746007" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b21002 SNOMED CT 251746007 = ICF b21002 Binocular acuity of near vision: the acuity function
        of both eyes together for near vision. Target SNOMED CT 4092478 (sctid 251746007) =, active RF2
        production. Exact 1:1 equivalence: identical clinical concept (binocular near visual acuity as
        an observable), literal FSN term match (binocular + near). High tier : exact term match and
        clear concept equivalence verified in both mirrors, no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified.
        mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
mapping "b21003.1" source="b21003" target="SNOMED_CT:251743004" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b21003 SNOMED CT 251743004 = ICF b21003 Monocular acuity of near vision: the acuity function
        of one eye for near vision (eye-unspecified — left OR right). Target SNOMED CT 4089822 (sctid
        251743004) =, active RF2 production. Broader: SNOMED CT's active monocular near-acuity observables
        are eye-specific (386711006, 386712004; the older 251744005/251745006 are inactive/D). The ICF
        source is laterality-unspecified, so no single eye-specific SNOMED CT concept matches; 251743004 is
