mapping "b2102.1" source="b2102" target="SNOMED_CT:281004000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target effect=omitted quality=60 {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b2102 SNOMED CT 281004000 = ICF b2102 Quality of vision functions: the visual functions
        underlying the quality of the visual image — encompasses b21020 light sensitivity, b21021 color
        vision, b21022 contrast sensitivity. This is a grouping/quality-of-vision function that has NO
        single direct SNOMED CT equivalent (the sub-functions b21020-b21022 each have exact SNOMED CT
        observables, but their parent grouping does not). Target SNOMED CT 4094031 (sctid 281004000) =,
        active — the broader parent visual-function observable that fully subsumes the quality-of-vision
        axis. Broader: the target is a true ancestor (all quality-of-vision functions are visual
        functions) but a multi-level climb and also covers acuity/field. Low tier : defensible
        best-available ancestor, but loose — no observable exists in SNOMED CT and the target is a deep
        climb; the b21020-b21022 children each get their own exact_match proposals. Recorded as broader
        (not no_match) because the visual-function observable is the defensible standard ancestor a
        reviewer would expect for a vision-quality grouping.
        """
}
mapping "b21020.1" source="b21020" target="SNOMED_CT:41701000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b21020 SNOMED CT 41701000 = ICF b21020 Light sensitivity: the visual functions of sensing a
        minimum amount of light (the minimum luminance generating a visual sensation) and adapting to
        varying light levels — i.e. scotopic/photopic sensitivity and dark adaptation as visual
        functions. Target SNOMED CT 4218321 (sctid 41701000) =, active RF2 production. Broader rather than
        exact: ICF b21020 spans BOTH the absolute light-detection threshold AND adaptation to changing
        light; SNOMED CT has no single observable, and captures only the adaptation half of b21020, not the
        absolute-threshold half. Because the chosen target covers only one component (adaptation) of a
        two-component source, the target does NOT fully subsume the source, so this is assessed as
        broader at low tier — it is the closest standard observable in the vision/light-sensitivity
        domain and fully contains one axis (adaptation) of the source, defensible as a reviewer lead.
        (90128006 rejected: it is a cutaneous/light-skin finding, not visual light sensitivity; 27073006
        rejected: a stimulus-property function, not visual light sensitivity.) The split-axis nature of
        b21020 keeps this at low confidence rather than exact.
        """
}
mapping "b21021.1" source="b21021" target="SNOMED_CT:271726001" relationship=equivalent {
