        visual-function residual. Target SNOMED CT 4094031 (sctid 281004000) =, active. Broader: the parent
        visual-function concept subsumes the unspecified source. Low tier: unspecified source forced up
        to the chapter parent; no specific clinical content to preserve. A defensible parent exists
        (unlike the targetless visual-quality residual), so broader-at-low-confidence rather than
        no_match.
        """
}
mapping "b215.1" source="b215" target="SNOMED_CT:414302002" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b215 SNOMED CT 414302002 = ICF functions of structures adjoining the eye (a grouping
        covering eyelid, extraocular/intraocular muscles, lacrimal glands, etc.). Target SNOMED CT 4185760
        (sctid 414302002) =, active. Broader: the target is the SNOMED CT eye-region-function grouping that
        subsumes this ICF grouping. Low tier: the source is itself a heterogeneous grouping (muscle +
        gland + lid functions) and the target is the only defensible grouping-level standard concept;
        one-level broader but the breadth mismatch is real. No single more-specific SNOMED CT concept
        covers the whole grouping.
        """
}
mapping "b2150.1" source="b2150" target="SNOMED_CT:4209008" relationship=partial_overlap {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b2150 SNOMED CT 4209008 = ICF functions of the internal (intraocular) muscles of the eye =
        sphincter/dilator pupillae (pupillary light response) AND ciliary muscle (accommodation). Target
        (sctid 56777005) =, active. Partial: the target covers only the pupillary axis of a
        two-component source; the accommodation (ciliary-muscle) axis has no separate SNOMED CT observable
        in the mirror. Per the boundary rule, a multi-part source mapped to one component is partial,
        not broader. Low tier: partial coverage with the second axis (accommodation) unrepresentable;
        cap at.
        """
}
